      "created_at": "2016-12-07T02:06:11Z",
      "updated_at": "2016-12-07T02:06:11Z",
      "body": "It should only be available to the installer of the Pi-hole application locally. No data leaves the Pi-hole unless you explicitly allow it (and that only happens when you run the debug command, you are provided with the directions of what information may be passed an where it is passed on to. You are given the option to not upload the debug log as well.)\r\n\r\nWe will be releasing an update soon that has the ability to password protect the web interface, and we have instructions on the Wiki how to turn off all logging and disable any use of the admin interface. \r\n\r\nI am not sure how this is a security or privacy breach?\r\n",
      "author_association": "MEMBER",
      "pin": null,
