      "created_at": "2016-12-07T11:34:28Z",
      "updated_at": "2016-12-07T11:35:31Z",
      "body": "Well, you surely don't expect the big browser companies to mention the possibility that there might be a custom DNS server in the network of the local user. That is something that (a) doesn't happen very often and (b) isn't easily understandable for the typical user (\"what is DNS?\").\r\nStill, this is somehow covered by \"your employer\" and \"your internet service provider\", since you are an active part of the internet service provider by providing a custom DNS server.\r\n\r\nThat is something you who has to make that clear to your girlfriend and everybody who uses your internet connection! You are right in the sense that you cannot expect them to know that the internet in your house is working differently than everywhere else. In their companies they may expect that there is something going on in the network which isn't transparent to the users. YOU have to make clear that something similar is going on in your network.",
      "author_association": "MEMBER",
      "pin": null,
